@startuml new-principle-cascade
title smaqit.new-principle — live registry-driven cascade

actor "User / Agent" as User
participant "smaqit.new-principle\n(skill — owns every\nTask call below)" as Skill
participant "smaqit.L0" as L0
participant "smaqit.L1" as L1
database "registry.json\n(base or extension scope)" as Registry
participant "smaqit.L2" as L2

note over L0, L1
  Neither holds a **Task** tool — they report
  back to the skill, they never chain into
  the next stage themselves. No nested
  agent-to-agent calls exist in this flow.
end note

User -> Skill : "add or refine a principle"
activate Skill

== Step 1: principle authoring ==
Skill -> L0 : Task call
activate L0
L0 -> L0 : detect scope\n(base: this repo /\nextension: consuming project)
L0 -> L0 : write principle to\nframework/*.md\nor .smaqit/framework/*.md
note right of L0
  Rejects an extension principle
  that merely restates base content.
end note
L0 --> Skill : scope + exact file path changed
deactivate L0

== Step 2: template/rules review ==
Skill -> L1 : Task call\n"does this principle change\nrequire a template/rules update?"
activate L1

alt L1 judges no update needed
  L1 --> Skill : "no update needed"
  deactivate L1
  Skill -> User : report — principle added,\nno cascade
else L1 updates a template or rules file
  L1 -> L1 : write templates/agents/*.template.md\nor templates/agents/compiled/*.rules.md\n(or the skills/ equivalents)
  L1 --> Skill : exact file path touched
  deactivate L1

  == Step 3: dependent lookup ==
  Skill -> Registry : registry get --depends-on <path>\n(plain Bash call, not Task)
  activate Registry
  note left of Registry
    Entries here were written by
    smaqit.L2 on every PAST compile —
    the only place the "who depends on
    this template/rules file" edge lives.
  end note
  Registry --> Skill : 0..N dependent entries
  deactivate Registry

  == Step 4: cascade recompilation ==
  loop for each dependent entry
    Skill -> L2 : Task call
    activate L2
    L2 -> L2 : recompile from the entry's\nrecorded sourceDefinition\n+ sourceTemplates
    L2 -> L2 : write .claude/agents/*.md\n+ .codex/agents/*.toml\nor skills/<name>/SKILL.md
    L2 -> Registry : registry put\n(fresh compiledHash + lastCompiled)
    activate Registry
    Registry --> L2
    deactivate Registry
    L2 --> Skill : recompiled
    deactivate L2
  end

  == Step 5: report ==
  Skill -> User : report — scope, template/rules\nfile touched, N dependents recompiled
end

deactivate Skill
@enduml
